    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> was the largest battle of the Napoleonic Wars, with about 560,000 soldiers, 2,200 artillery pieces and 133,000 casualties, and arguably the deciding battle of the wars.</li><li>Most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s army consisted of teenagers and inexperienced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conscription">conscripts</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> and Württemberg troops went over to the Coalition during the fighting.</li><li>After the battle the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a> was dissolved, the Coalition invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in early 1814, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> abdicated on 6 April.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>On 19 October a corporal ignited the fuses of the only bridge over the Elster at 1:00 in the afternoon, while it was still crowded with retreating French troops. Marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jozef-poniatowski">Poniatowski</a>, wounded, was among those who drowned.</p></aside>
    </section>

